  "description": "I1 probe for prop:jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.  Verifies for n ∈ {3, 4, 5} and ℓ ∈ {1, …, n}: (i) the elementary symmetric polynomial P_ℓ = e_ℓ(J_1, …, J_n) acts as a scalar on V_λ (all SYT diagonal entries equal — centrality); (ii) the scalar value matches the closed form c_ℓ(λ) = e_ℓ({q^{2c(□)} : □ ∈ λ}).  Uses JM-eigenvalue diagonal action on the Hoefsmit basis.  Tested across 19 irreps (3 + 5 + 11 partitions of n = 3, 4, 5).  Residues are at the arithmetic floor and are therefore a statement about the working precision, not about the mathematics: see max_centrality_residue / max_closed_form_residue, measured at the live compute precision (mp.dps = 70). The previous wording, '~1e-50 (mpmath 50 dps)', was written when the default was 50 dps and was stale by 20 orders once the floor moved to 70.",
